# Build output.
#
# The repo was rebuilt clean once already to purge committed binaries. The
# front ends are 5-35 MB each and a bare `git add .` puts every one of them
# back, so the binary names are listed explicitly as well as bin/.
bin/
/capture
/captureui
/crawl
/crawlui
/mapview
/pathfinder
/pfconnect
/pfterm
/pfvault
/reach
/reachmaps
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.test
*.out

# Coverage and profiling.
coverage.out
coverage.html
*.prof
covdata/

# Local toolchain scratch. floor.local carries container-absolute replace
# paths and must never ship; go.work overrides the module graph.
scripts/floor.local
go.work
go.work.sum
/vendor/

# Run artifacts. Crawl maps, capture stores and saved runs all carry real
# device names when they come off a real network, which is exactly what must
# not land in the repo. lab-map.json is the one committed fixture and is
# re-added below.
*-map.json
*.graphml
maps/
pf_maps/
captures/
runs/
!lab-map.json

# Credentials. Never committed under any circumstances: the vault is
# encrypted but the bindings file names devices, and known_hosts names hosts.
vault.json
*.vault.json
*.bindings.json
known_hosts
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~

